00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:12.819
That's why we do what we do. So, on occasion, we can have conflicts between

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:22.339
gators or crocodiles that are going to become used to human population and are going to become

00:17:22.339 --> 00:17:28.819
problem animals. One of our preferred solutions, whenever possible, is to basically take those

00:17:28.819 --> 00:17:36.180
animals and relocate them within a more natural setting so they don't bother human populations

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:42.420
anymore. So, that specific study was kind of like a test study to figure out, hey,

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:48.739
is that actually a good solution for us to do that? And we are trying to figure out,

00:17:48.739 --> 00:17:53.459
depending on how far away we relocate them, how effective are those techniques?

00:17:54.260 --> 00:18:01.540
So, it turns out that those animals are incredibly good at finding their way back,

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:10.339
a lot better than I am. We would move them by, you know, a couple dozen miles, and they would

00:18:10.339 --> 00:18:18.500
