I, my job here is to kind of, like, help with this connection between ecologists and management

00:21:26.579 --> 00:21:32.180
and stats. I'm not as good in ecology as a pure statistician. I'm not as good in stats as a pure,

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:36.500
sorry, I'm not as good in ecology as a pure ecologist, and I'm not as good as, in stats,

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:42.660
as a pure statistician. But I'm a lot better in stats as an ecologist and a lot better in ecology

00:21:42.739 --> 00:21:49.380
as a pure statistician. So, I'm able to make this bridge. And coming here as a public sector also

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:55.699
helped me make that connection with management and hopefully, like, one level removed with the

00:21:55.699 --> 00:22:02.099
general public. It does come with some difficulties in the sense that, yeah, we deal with

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:12.339
potentially sensitive topics, and what we do has consequences. And that's really important.

00:22:12.339 --> 00:22:18.819
But in my position, what we try to do at our agency is to provide the right information

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:25.780
in the right format at the right time. So, basically, use the most novel, most strongly,

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:30.500
like, the strongest possible science so we can better inform our decisions.

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:38.500
And then somebody's going to, somebody that has a bigger picture of, like, of the situation than I

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:45.219
do can come and just, okay, look at this is what my stakeholders and the public want. This is the

00:22:45.219 --> 00:22:49.780
current status of appropriation. So, it can be, like, fisheries when we have to figure out, like,

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:55.140
can we fish this species at this time of year? How much can we get? That can be related to just

00:22:55.140 --> 00:23:01.380
general population management, species, dealing with deer, like, white-tailed deer, or turkey,

00:23:01.459 --> 00:23:12.180
these kind of things. So, based on my experience, I think that it can be more challenging to get,

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:18.739
to collect data, because there's so much of it. We can't, you know, we're trying to just deal with

00:23:18.739 --> 00:23:24.099
the whole ecosystem in Florida, and we're not, you know, disconnected from the rest of the U.S.

